# K01 witness (steps/k01-selector-identity-20261001.md §6), negative: the same candidate
# as unit_occ_selector_unused_first, but the Consumer's use is `[0]x` -- its required
# occurrence-0 x is a size_t and the candidate's is an int, so the admission must be
# refused even though the bare-last Consumer of this candidate is legal.  This is a
# compile-time refusal at the call site, not a resolution refusal.
Pair: (size_t: x 10U; size_t: x 20U)
Tri: (int: x 7; size_t: x 20U; size_t: x 30U)
fn: firstToo (Pair: v) int
    size_t: got
    got: v\[0]x
    return: (cast: (int) (got))
end: firstToo
t: merge Tri
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: firstToo(t); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
